1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,419
What is i to the power
one hundred and three?

2
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:05,095
It looks like a monster.

3
00:00:05,095 --> 00:00:08,255
i times i times i, one
hundred and three times.

4
00:00:08,655 --> 00:00:12,178
You can answer it in three
seconds, without a calculator.

5
00:00:12,628 --> 00:00:15,629
Aarav found the secret in
his notebook last night.

6
00:00:15,629 --> 00:00:18,412
He wrote down the powers of i, one by one.

7
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:20,915
i, minus one, minus i, one.

8
00:00:20,915 --> 00:00:23,020
Then i again, minus one again.

9
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:25,954
After four lines, the
list started to repeat.

10
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:27,676
Why every four?

11
00:00:27,676 --> 00:00:29,012
Let us find out.

12
00:00:29,662 --> 00:00:33,240
Last time we met i, the number
whose square is minus one.

13
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:38,668
In symbols, i is the square root of
minus one, so i squared is minus one.

14
00:00:38,668 --> 00:00:40,887
It is called the imaginary unit.

15
00:00:41,287 --> 00:00:43,163
Imaginary is only a name.

16
00:00:43,163 --> 00:00:44,884
It does not mean fake.

17
00:00:44,884 --> 00:00:49,013
The symbol i was first used by
the great mathematician Euler.

18
00:00:49,663 --> 00:00:52,350
Now build the powers, one step at a time.

19
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:54,991
Each new power is the last one, times i.

20
00:00:55,341 --> 00:00:56,241
Step one.

21
00:00:56,086 --> 00:00:58,068
i to the power one is just i.

22
00:00:58,818 --> 00:00:59,718
Step two.

23
00:00:59,622 --> 00:01:01,291
i squared is minus one.

24
00:01:01,291 --> 00:01:02,900
That is the definition.

25
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,661
Step three.

26
00:01:04,661 --> 00:01:06,990
i cubed is i squared times i.

27
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:09,320
Minus one times i is minus i.

28
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:10,970
Step four.

29
00:01:10,964 --> 00:01:14,045
i to the four is i
squared times i squared.

30
00:01:14,045 --> 00:01:16,428
Minus one times minus one is one.

31
00:01:17,178 --> 00:01:18,078
Step five.

32
00:01:18,043 --> 00:01:20,889
i to the five is i to the four times i.

33
00:01:20,889 --> 00:01:22,282
One times i is i.

34
00:01:22,282 --> 00:01:24,132
We are back at the start.

35
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:27,170
Now watch the same thing as a picture.

36
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:30,392
Put one on the right and
minus one on the left.

37
00:01:30,392 --> 00:01:33,157
Put i straight up, and
minus i straight down.

38
00:01:33,557 --> 00:01:37,952
Multiplying by i turns a point
a quarter turn, anticlockwise.

39
00:01:38,352 --> 00:01:41,459
Start at one, and let
the power n count up.

40
00:01:41,459 --> 00:01:43,634
A quarter turn takes one to i.

41
00:01:43,634 --> 00:01:45,698
Another takes i to minus one.

42
00:01:45,698 --> 00:01:46,781
Then minus i.

43
00:01:46,781 --> 00:01:48,124
Then home to one.

44
00:01:48,524 --> 00:01:51,046
Four quarter turns make one full turn.

45
00:01:51,046 --> 00:01:53,774
That is why the powers repeat every four.

46
00:01:54,424 --> 00:01:56,141
So here is the shortcut.

47
00:01:56,141 --> 00:01:57,908
Divide the power by four.

48
00:01:57,908 --> 00:01:59,714
Only the remainder matters.

49
00:02:00,114 --> 00:02:01,985
Remainder zero gives one.

50
00:02:01,985 --> 00:02:03,694
Remainder one gives i.

51
00:02:03,694 --> 00:02:05,898
Remainder two gives minus one.

52
00:02:05,898 --> 00:02:08,102
Remainder three gives minus i.

53
00:02:08,702 --> 00:02:10,000
Back to the hook.

54
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,885
One hundred and three is four
times twenty five, plus three.

55
00:02:13,885 --> 00:02:17,982
Remainder three, so i to the one
hundred and three is minus i.

56
00:02:18,632 --> 00:02:20,261
It even works backwards.

57
00:02:20,261 --> 00:02:23,654
i to the minus one is a
quarter turn the other way.

58
00:02:23,654 --> 00:02:24,801
It is minus i.

59
00:02:25,451 --> 00:02:26,351
Your turn.

60
00:02:26,313 --> 00:02:30,208
Is i to the power twenty two
equal to one, or minus one?

61
00:02:30,208 --> 00:02:31,427
Pause and think.

62
00:02:34,627 --> 00:02:35,554
Minus one!

63
00:02:35,554 --> 00:02:38,568
Twenty two is four times five, plus two.

64
00:02:38,568 --> 00:02:40,751
Remainder two gives minus one.

65
00:02:41,401 --> 00:02:42,536
Remember this.

66
00:02:42,536 --> 00:02:47,404
The powers of i go round in
fours: i, minus one, minus i, one.

67
00:02:48,104 --> 00:02:50,864
Now, square roots of negative numbers.

68
00:02:50,864 --> 00:02:55,708
Minus i squared is also minus one,
because minus times minus is plus.

69
00:02:56,108 --> 00:02:59,628
So minus one has two square
roots, i and minus i.

70
00:03:00,028 --> 00:03:03,754
But the symbol, root minus
one, means just one of them: i.

71
00:03:03,754 --> 00:03:07,068
In the same way, root four
means two, not minus two.

72
00:03:07,668 --> 00:03:12,105
So for any positive number a,
root minus a is root a times i.

73
00:03:12,105 --> 00:03:14,156
Root minus nine is three i.

74
00:03:14,756 --> 00:03:15,775
Quick check.

75
00:03:15,775 --> 00:03:17,225
Root minus sixteen.

76
00:03:17,225 --> 00:03:19,673
Is it four i, or minus four i?

77
00:03:19,673 --> 00:03:20,966
Pause and think.

78
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:25,066
Four i!

79
00:03:24,887 --> 00:03:28,752
The root symbol picks the one
root: root sixteen times i.

80
00:03:29,402 --> 00:03:31,138
Now, one worked example.

81
00:03:31,488 --> 00:03:36,501
Find i to the ten, plus i to the
eleven, plus i to the twelve, plus i to

82
00:03:36,501 --> 00:03:37,518
the thirteen.

83
00:03:38,018 --> 00:03:38,918
Step one.

84
00:03:38,864 --> 00:03:42,805
Ten leaves remainder two, so
i to the ten is minus one.

85
00:03:43,555 --> 00:03:44,455
Step two.

86
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:48,828
Eleven leaves remainder three,
so i to the eleven is minus i.

87
00:03:49,578 --> 00:03:50,486
Step three.

88
00:03:50,486 --> 00:03:54,522
Twelve leaves remainder zero, and
thirteen leaves remainder one.

89
00:03:54,522 --> 00:03:56,200
They give one, and i.

90
00:03:56,950 --> 00:03:57,855
Step four.

91
00:03:57,855 --> 00:03:58,755
Add them.

92
00:03:58,709 --> 00:04:01,707
Minus one, minus i, plus one, plus i.

93
00:04:01,707 --> 00:04:03,081
Everything cancels.

94
00:04:03,081 --> 00:04:04,424
The sum is zero.

95
00:04:05,174 --> 00:04:09,707
On the picture, the four moves go round
a square and end where they began.

96
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:12,124
Any four powers in a row add to zero.

97
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:14,239
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:14,589 --> 00:04:19,183
Many students write root minus four
times root minus nine as root thirty

99
00:04:19,183 --> 00:04:20,728
six, which is six.

100
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:26,028
But the rule root a times root b equals
root a b breaks when both numbers

101
00:04:26,028 --> 00:04:27,101
are negative.

102
00:04:27,101 --> 00:04:32,379
Root minus four is two i, root minus
nine is three i, and two i times three

103
00:04:32,379 --> 00:04:33,957
i is six i squared.

104
00:04:33,957 --> 00:04:35,418
That is minus six.

105
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:37,625
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:37,625 --> 00:04:42,743
In JEE Main, in September twenty
twenty, a power of i had to equal one.

107
00:04:42,743 --> 00:04:44,519
And in PUC board exams.

108
00:04:45,119 --> 00:04:46,285
Exam level now.

109
00:04:46,285 --> 00:04:51,056
What is the sum of i to the n, for n
from one to two thousand and twenty

110
00:04:51,056 --> 00:04:51,956
six?

111
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,775
Pause and solve.

112
00:04:58,175 --> 00:04:59,606
The answer is C.

113
00:04:59,606 --> 00:05:01,092
Minus one plus i.

114
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:04,228
Any four powers in a row add to zero.

115
00:05:04,728 --> 00:05:09,641
Two thousand and twenty six is four
times five hundred and six, plus two.

116
00:05:09,641 --> 00:05:13,923
So the first two thousand and
twenty four terms make full cycles.

117
00:05:13,923 --> 00:05:15,283
They add to zero.

118
00:05:15,783 --> 00:05:17,229
Two terms are left.

119
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:22,068
i to the two thousand and twenty five
is i, and i to the two thousand and

120
00:05:22,068 --> 00:05:23,825
twenty six is minus one.

121
00:05:23,825 --> 00:05:25,903
The sum is minus one plus i.

122
00:05:26,503 --> 00:05:27,967
Here is your recap.

123
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:29,472
Screenshot this card.

124
00:05:32,672 --> 00:05:35,509
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

125
00:05:35,909 --> 00:05:36,809
One.

126
00:05:36,415 --> 00:05:38,518
What is i to the power fifty?

127
00:05:39,418 --> 00:05:40,318
Two.

128
00:05:40,002 --> 00:05:44,724
Why is root minus four times
root minus nine not equal to six?

129
00:05:45,624 --> 00:05:46,524
Three.

130
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:48,237
What is i to the minus two?

131
00:05:49,337 --> 00:05:53,699
Next time: an address with two
parts, which street and which floor.

132
00:05:53,699 --> 00:05:57,423
Every complex number has a real
part and an imaginary part.
